 "domain": "Measurement",
 "standard_code": "AC9M8M02",
 "standard_url": "https://v9.australiancurriculum.edu.au/f-10-curriculum/learning-areas/mathematics",
 "standard_text": "solve problems involving the volume and capacity of right prisms using appropriate units",
 "meta_desc": "Free Year 8 maths worksheets on volume and capacity for the Australian Curriculum (AC9M8M02): converting cm³, mL, L, m³ and kL, capacity of tanks and pools, prisms with composite cross-sections and missing dimensions. 100 questions with an answer key.",
 "key_big": "1 cm³ = 1 mL, 1000 cm³ = 1 L and 1 m³ = 1000 L = 1 kL.",
 "key_sub": "Volume of a prism = area of the cross-section × length.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How it works</h2><p>Volume of any right prism = <b>area of the cross-section × length</b>. For a rectangular prism this is length × width × height.</p><p><b>Capacity</b> is how much a container holds. Link volume and capacity with: <b>1 cm³ = 1 mL</b>, <b>1000 cm³ = 1 L</b> and <b>1 m³ = 1000 L = 1 kL</b>.</p><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Find the capacity in litres of a tank 50 cm by 30 cm by 40 cm.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>50 × 30 × 40 = 60 000 cm³.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>60 000 ÷ 1000.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 60 L</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>A pool is 10 m by 5 m by 1.2 m deep. How many kilolitres does it hold?</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>10 × 5 × 1.2 = 60 m³.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>1 m³ = 1 kL.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 60 kL</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Dividing by 100 instead of 1000 when changing cm³ to litres.</li><li>Forgetting that 1 m³ is 1000 L, not 100 L.</li><li>Adding the dimensions instead of multiplying them.</li><li>Finding the area of the cross-section but not multiplying by the length.</li></ul>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What is the difference between volume and capacity?",
   "a": "Volume is the space an object takes up. Capacity is how much a container can hold. They are linked: 1 cm³ holds 1 mL."
  },
  {
   "q": "How many litres are in a cubic metre?",
   "a": "1000 litres, which is 1 kilolitre."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do I find the capacity of a tank in litres?",
   "a": "Find the volume in cm³ and divide by 1000, or find it in m³ and multiply by 1000."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do I find the volume of a prism with an L-shaped cross-section?",
   "a": "Find the area of the L-shape (split it into rectangles), then multiply by the length of the prism."
  }
 ],
